    <span class="cs-section-label">The Challenge</span>
    <h2>Mike Was Drowning</h2>
    <p>Mike runs Capital Wealth Management, a growing financial advisory practice with 80+ active clients. By every external measure, business was good. Revenue was climbing. Referrals were flowing in.</p>
    <p>But internally? Mike was working 70-hour weeks and still falling behind. The symptoms were everywhere:</p>

    <ul class="pain-list">
      <li><span class="pain-icon">&#10007;</span> 200+ emails hitting his inbox daily &mdash; client requests, compliance notices, vendor follow-ups &mdash; and he was manually sorting every one</li>
      <li><span class="pain-icon">&#10007;</span> Compliance deadlines tracked on sticky notes and memory. One slip could mean regulatory action.</li>
      <li><span class="pain-icon">&#10007;</span> Client follow-ups falling through the cracks. New leads going cold because he couldn't respond fast enough.</li>
      <li><span class="pain-icon">&#10007;</span> Zero content marketing. No blog, no newsletter, no social presence. Too busy putting out fires to build the brand.</li>
      <li><span class="pain-icon">&#10007;</span> Missing his kids' events. Working weekends. Burning out.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Mike had tried hiring an assistant. Two, actually. Both lasted less than six months. The learning curve was too steep, the volume too high, and the compliance knowledge gap too wide.</p>
  </div>

